# --- Node ---
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# --- Project data (never commit datasets or model files) ---
data/datasets/
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# --- Evaluation data (M3) ---
# The CSVs are DERIVED: `python -m eval.build` regenerates them byte-for-byte from the
# seeded generators in eval/datasets/, which ARE committed. Committing 3.5 MB of data
# that a 400-line generator reproduces exactly would add weight and no information --
# and the generator is the artefact worth reviewing, because it states which effects
# were deliberately built in.
eval/data/

# The dataset ids are UUIDs minted on whichever machine ran the build, so this file
# means nothing anywhere else. Recreated by `python -m eval.build`.
eval/answers/registry.json

# NOTE: eval/answers/*.json IS committed on purpose. It is the ground truth every
# benchmark score is measured against, and keeping it in the repo is what makes a
# generator change show up as a reviewable diff of exactly which answers moved,
# rather than as a silently different score.

# --- Internal working documents (not project documentation) ---
# These describe how the work is being planned and learned, not how the system works.
# The durable content lives in docs/decisions.md and the README roadmap.
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
AI_Data_Intelligence_Platform_MVP_Roadmap.md

# NOTE: scripts/_bench_raw/*.json IS committed on purpose — it is the raw evidence
# behind every number in docs/benchmarking.md, and a reader should be able to check it.

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
